{"doc_id":"REPORT-news_r-00476-00001","summaries":{"A":{"adequacy":2,"critical_unsupported":1,"critical_omission":1,"wrong_unit_qualifier":0,"entity_relation":1,"fluency":3,"utility":2,"evidence":["「하루 한장 파닉스」 시리즈는 하루 한 장씩 40일 간 알파벳과 자음과 모음의 소릿값을 익히는 파닉스 프로그램","「하루 한장 영단어」는 쉽고 효과적으로 영단어를 학습할 수 있도록 돕는 교재다."],"reason":"The summary calls the series an 'elementary/middle/high reference book' again, which misdescribes it. It also says both the phonics and vocabulary series are the 40-day phonics program, which merges two different products. It leaves out the vocabulary book's content and the 4+1 structure."},"B":{"adequacy":2,"critical_unsupported":1,"critical_omission":0,"wrong_unit_qualifier":1,"entity_relation":1,"fluency":3,"utility":2,"evidence":["「하루 한장 English BITE 파닉스」","마지막 5일차에는 한 주 동안 학습한 내용을 다시 복습할 수 있는 〈4+1〉 시스템"],"reason":"The summary says the whole 'English BITE' series is the 40-day phonics program, which is a scope error. It also says the manager built the 4+1 system to resolve the school-versus-academy English gap. The source doesn't support that causal claim, and the quote is cut off. Its coverage of the phonics and vocabulary details is reasonable."},"C":{"adequacy":2,"critical_unsupported":1,"critical_omission":1,"wrong_unit_qualifier":1,"entity_relation":1,"fluency":3,"utility":2,"evidence":["학부모들의 적극적인 요청을 수렴해 개발, 출간했다.","하루 한 장씩 40일 간"],"reason":"The summary attributes the development background to the manager, but the source gives it as the publisher's statement. It drops the phonics 40-day period and the target ages. It also leaves out the grade guidance and the 4+1 system."},"D":{"adequacy":3,"critical_unsupported":0,"critical_omission":0,"wrong_unit_qualifier":1,"entity_relation":1,"fluency":3,"utility":4,"evidence":["하루 한 장씩 40일 간 알파벳과 자음과 모음의 소릿값을 익히는 파닉스 프로그램","매주 1~4일까지는 개별 학습으로 진행되며, 마지막 5일차에는 ... 〈4+1〉 시스템"],"reason":"The summary covers the phonics details, the vocabulary numbers and the 4+1 structure accurately. It blurs the series with the phonics book, and it credits the manager with the parent-request development statement. The sentences are long and awkward."}}}
